      "writtenOn": "2020-06-26T23:56:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it an error to provide more sources?  Could we pass the first source file to rustc but depend on the rest?\n\nOnly specifying one source file will be a problem for remoting the compile with RBE.  RBE needs to know the list of source files to send to the remote builder, ideally from the Android.bp file but possibly from scanning the source files locally if necessary with something like clang-scan-deps.  We could emulate that locally by sandboxing the rustc compile so it can only see listed source files.",
      "parentUuid": "ce082488_b83730a2",
      "revId": "3efa86a963d2fa3980902c8dbe53af1840b57418",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "47e72e3f_8d9f716a",
        "filename": "rust/compiler.go",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 85,
