        "id": 1052399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-29T19:28:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, current rust_* modules reject multiple files in \"srcs\".\nThat\u0027s good as rustc only accepts one.\nWe should catch errors that specify multiple files in \"srcs\".\n\nThis situation is like C/C++ source files that include\nother generated files or header files. The generated files\nare not passed to C/C++ compilers.\nShouldn\u0027t RBE already handle those cases?\n\nEven without generated files, rustc will import other\nmodule source files in the src or sub directories.\nThat will fail if RBE does not copy all files in source tree, right?",
      "parentUuid": "41ccbcd6_dc679e6e",
      "revId": "3efa86a963d2fa3980902c8dbe53af1840b57418",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
