      "writtenOn": "2020-06-29T21:50:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two parts of this change. (1) allow a Rust binary to be used in a genrule module, (2) allow a Rust module to depend on other genrule module, which may or may not use Rust tool. These are only current C/C++ features.\n\nWhether the genrule output file is copied or not to other places is an independent issue. If RBE does not like generated file copied back to source tree, users can change their genrule and source code to include the generated file from the out directory. That has been used in the pending CL to generate Rust bindings for libselinux.",
      "parentUuid": "4805c2e1_12c9413a",
